.docs/decisions/0118-dailyos-as-ai-harness-principles-and-residual-gaps.md:95:**Proposal.** During [DOS-7](https://linear.app/a8c/issue/DOS-7) design review, specify `intelligence_claims` as append-only with respect to assertion changes. Concretely: add `claim_sequence` (monotonic per `(entity_id, claim_type, field_path)`), `previous_claim_id` (nullable FK), `superseded_at` (nullable), `superseded_by` (nullable FK), `retraction_reason` (nullable enum). Keep the drafted `trust_version` for trust-only revisions. Prune policy: retain last N assertion values per field plus aggregate stability metric (flap rate, assertion-age, distinct-value count). Bounded growth — under 10K entities × ~20 claim types × ~1 change/week, pruned history fits well under 10M rows.
